    "probe_text": "Read complete. Here is the full ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, exactly as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented by the function classes. Every step runs under a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the very end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **`authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`** \u2014 the whole endpoint requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role (else 403).\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n\n- **Bean validation** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, runs before the method body; failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**):\n  - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, `@Size 1..30`\n  - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`, `@Size 1..30`\n  - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*` (non-blank), `@Size 1..255`\n  - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*` (non-blank), `@Size 1..80`\n  - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1..20`\n  - `email` \u2014 optional, `@Size max 255`\n  - `postcode` \u2014 optional, `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$` (shape only: exactly 4 digits)\n- **Side-effect:** maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity and publishes it (plus republishes the DTO so later steps can read create-only flags like `sharesHousehold`).\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation:** if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**. (Checked against the raw supplied value, before defaulting.)\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`\n- **Side-effect:** if `registrationDate` is absent, default it to the server's current date; then if it lands on Sat/Sun, roll it forward to the following Monday. Stored on the entity (later daily-limit/membership logic sees this adjusted date).\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`\n- **Side-effect + validation:** normalize telephone to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+`/country code, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; require 8\u201315 digits, and matching national length for `+61`=9 / `+1`=10). Unparseable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**. Valid value is stored on the entity.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerEmail`\n- **Side-effect + validation:** if email absent, no-op; if present it must match a basic address regex else `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**; otherwise lower-cased and stored.\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`\n- **Validation:** if email present and its domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerAddress`\n- **Side-effect + validation:** normalize address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). If blank after normalization \u2192 `InvalidAddressException` \u2192 **400**; else stored.\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `RejectInvalidPostcode`\n- **Validation:** if postcode present, check it against the region derived from `city` (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any). Out of range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignOwnerHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** derive deterministic `householdId` = first 12 UPPER-hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`. Left null if last name or postcode missing (household of one).\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`\n- **Validation (queries all existing owners):**\n  - exact `identityKey` match (telephone|email|householdId) with an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409** (never bypassed);\n  - same computed `householdId` as an existing owner \u2192 **409**, *unless* the request set `sharesHousehold`.\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`\n- **Validation:** if the (normalized) city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `RejectOwnerDailyLimit`\n- **Validation:** if \u2265 100 owners already exist for the same (adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect:** if not a declared household member, set `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest existing owner sharing last name + postcode but with a *different* telephone (soft-duplicate flag; create still proceeds).\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`\n- **Side-effect:** set `householdSize` = existing members sharing `householdId` + 1 (or 1 if no household).\n\n## Step 15 \u2014 `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from the postcode (else `UNKNOWN`) and HASH8 is the first 8 UPPER-hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n## Step 16 \u2014 `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** set `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first + last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## Step 17 \u2014 `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning`\n- **Side-effect:** set `bulkSignupWarning` = true when existing owners for the same business day exceed 80.\n\n## Step 18 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persist the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n## Step 19 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** emit an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n\n## Step 20 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** send **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n---\n\n**Note on ordering rationale baked into the wiring:** body/bean validation happens first; the future-date check runs before defaulting so it sees the raw value; email/address are normalized before their reject checks; `householdId` is computed before the duplicate check that depends on it; and all reject checks run before the assign/persist steps so nothing is written for a rejected request (and the single transaction rolls back regardless)."
